      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.41,
          "end": 4.78,
          "en": "So we saw how we can build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.78,
          "end": 8.23,
          "en": "and deploy an app with Expo in the managed workflow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.23,
          "end": 9.52,
          "en": "which was pretty convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.52,
          "end": 11.53,
          "en": "Now, let's say we have an app, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.53,
          "end": 14.12,
          "en": "built with the React Native CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.12,
          "end": 16.3,
          "en": "Here I'm not using any native modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.3,
          "end": 18.32,
          "en": "but if I were, I would have, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.32,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "have updated my Android and iOS configuration files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 23.43,
          "en": "to request the right permissions and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 27.27,
          "en": "And I showed all of that in the non-Expo module earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.27,
          "end": 28.103,
          "en": "in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.103,
          "end": 29.72,
          "en": "So now let's say we're happy with the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.72,
          "end": 32.47,
          "en": "and we want to publish it to the Apple App Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.47,
          "end": 34.12,
          "en": "and the Google Play Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.12,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "Now, the official React Native docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 37.67,
          "en": "are a great place to get started with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.67,
          "end": 40.08,
          "en": "There in the documentation under Guides,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.08,
          "end": 42.69,
          "en": "you also find this Running On Device guide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.69,
          "end": 45.02,
          "en": "where you can learn how you build your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.02,
          "end": 46.84,
          "en": "for iOS or Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 46.84,
          "end": 49.31,
          "en": "on the different operating systems you might be working on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 49.31,
          "end": 52.47,
          "en": "Important, you can only build for iOS on macOS now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.47,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "Linux and Windows don't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 56.14,
          "en": "because now we're not building the app in the cloud",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 56.14,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "as we did with Expo but locally on our machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 61.43,
          "en": "and there Apple has this restriction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 61.43,
          "end": 63.7,
          "en": "that you can only build iOS apps on a Mac.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.7,
          "end": 65.45,
          "en": "It is what it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 65.45,
          "end": 68.1,
          "en": "So now what you need now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.1,
          "end": 69.92,
          "en": "is an Apple Developer account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 69.92,
          "end": 72.49,
          "en": "Right now, not necessarily a paid one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 72.49,
          "end": 73.45,
          "en": "just to build the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 73.45,
          "end": 75.13,
          "en": "however, if you want to build it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 75.13,
          "end": 77.53,
          "en": "for the App Stores, you need a paid one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 77.53,
          "end": 79.78999999999999,
          "en": "as mentioned earlier in this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 79.78999999999999,
          "end": 82.57,
          "en": "So you should set up such a Apple Developer account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 82.57,
          "end": 84.84,
          "en": "and then open your project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 88.3,
          "en": "your iOS project to be precise with Xcode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.3,
          "end": 91.14,
          "en": "There you can click open another project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 95.047,
          "en": "go into your project folder, there to the iOS folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 95.047,
          "end": 99.94,
          "en": "and there select this xc-workspace folder or file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 99.94,
          "end": 101.6,
          "en": "to open this with Xcode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 101.6,
          "end": 104.11,
          "en": "This opens your project, your iOS project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.11,
          "end": 107.473,
          "en": "which includes your React Native code, of course, in Xcode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "Now it's there where you now configure this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 113.27000000000001,
          "en": "where you set up your identifier, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 113.27000000000001,
          "end": 115.84,
          "en": "That's this inverse URL I was talking about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 115.84,
          "end": 119.667,
          "en": "which could be com.academind.rnnoexpotest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 122.978,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "Something like this where you set version numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 127.87,
          "en": "which your users will see and your build number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 127.87,
          "end": 130.98,
          "en": "which can simply be a number that you increment here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 130.98,
          "end": 133.13,
          "en": "where you should choose automatically managed sign in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 133.13,
          "end": 135.29,
          "en": "and where you now need to choose a team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.29,
          "end": 136.49,
          "en": "which should be shown here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 136.49,
          "end": 138.28,
          "en": "If not, add an account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 141.7,
          "en": "and there log in with your Apple ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 141.7,
          "end": 144.963,
          "en": "to add your Apple Developer account as an account here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 145.827,
          "end": 148.06,
          "en": "And thereafter, you should be able to choose your team here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 148.06,
          "end": 150.98,
          "en": "which will be required for automatically signing the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 150.98,
          "end": 154.19,
          "en": "which will then be done by Apple so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 154.19,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "You can, in general, configure your app here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 158.96,
          "en": "and prepare it for deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 158.96,
          "end": 161.24,
          "en": "and one important configuration is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 161.24,
          "end": 163.76,
          "en": "related to the icons you wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 163.76,
          "end": 166.61,
          "en": "In Expo, we set up the icons conveniently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 166.61,
          "end": 168.76,
          "en": "in a configuration and Expo generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 168.76,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "all the icons for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "Now it won't work like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 175.88,
          "en": "Now you need to set up these icons on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 175.88,
          "end": 179.43,
          "en": "And you do this by clicking on this little arrow here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 179.43,
          "end": 181.58,
          "en": "which takes you to the assets catalog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 182.93,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "and there you can now provide icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 187.64,
          "en": "and you need to provide icons in different sizes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 187.64,
          "end": 189.17,
          "en": "as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 189.17,
          "end": 191.54,
          "en": "Now, obviously, that was a convenient thing by Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 191.54,
          "end": 193.4,
          "en": "It did create these icons for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 193.4,
          "end": 196.173,
          "en": "and you didn't have to manually create all these icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 199.36,
          "en": "Attached, however, you find the icon's ZIP file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 199.36,
          "end": 202.53,
          "en": "which includes icons you can drag and drop in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 204.03300000000002,
          "en": "So that's what I'll now do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 207.57,
          "en": "And the icons are labeled such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 207.57,
          "end": 210.373,
          "en": "that it should be clear what you have to drag where.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 212.74,
          "end": 215.71,
          "en": "And with it, you've got the icons configured.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 215.71,
          "end": 218.66,
          "en": "You also might want to configure the launch screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 218.66,
          "end": 220.32,
          "en": "For that, you can expand this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 220.32,
          "end": 223.203,
          "en": "and there you find this LaunchScreen ZIP file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 224.37,
          "end": 228.07,
          "en": "This in the end allows you to customize your launch screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 228.07,
          "end": 231.29,
          "en": "There you can add new widgets to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 231.29,
          "end": 232.35,
          "en": "drag images into it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 232.35,
          "end": 234.8,
          "en": "change the text you see here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 234.8,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "and configure the launch screen in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 240.313,
          "en": "You can learn more about this in the Xcode docs, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 241.25,
          "end": 243.14,
          "en": "And once you did configure all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 243.14,
          "end": 245.19,
          "en": "you can build your app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 245.19,
          "end": 248.54,
          "en": "For that, you can also, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 248.54,
          "end": 250.04,
          "en": "test it on a simulator first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 250.04,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "by choosing a simulator version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 253.53,
          "en": "then clicking the play button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 253.53,
          "end": 255.15,
          "en": "and this will now build your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 255.15,
          "end": 256.62,
          "en": "and run it on the simulator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 256.62,
          "end": 259.88,
          "en": "Thereafter, of course, we can also build it for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 259.88,
          "end": 261.98,
          "en": "Let's just see whether this now all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 263.85,
          "end": 266.55,
          "en": "It launches this bundler process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 269.58,
          "en": "which you already saw earlier for this standalone app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 269.58,
          "end": 271.31,
          "en": "because, of course, that's still part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 271.31,
          "end": 273.62,
          "en": "of the development experience here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 273.62,
          "end": 275.683,
          "en": "It's still a React Native app after all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 276.61,
          "end": 278.89300000000003,
          "en": "which you use for building this native app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 279.99,
          "end": 283.09000000000003,
          "en": "And now it has succeeded and it launches the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 283.09000000000003,
          "end": 284.1,
          "en": "on a simulator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 284.1,
          "end": 285.4,
          "en": "Now, I'm not too interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 285.4,
          "end": 288.8,
          "en": "in the app there because I well, only have a very basic app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 288.8,
          "end": 290.55,
          "en": "which doesn't do anything fancy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 290.55,
          "end": 292.39300000000003,
          "en": "but this proves that building works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 293.43,
          "end": 294.43,
          "en": "Now, in the official docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 294.43,
          "end": 295.55,
          "en": "if you scroll down further,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 295.55,
          "end": 297.52,
          "en": "still in this Running On Device section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 297.52,
          "end": 299.01,
          "en": "you also learn how to build your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 299.01,
          "end": 302.04,
          "en": "for production if it's a non-Expo app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 302.04,
          "end": 304.49,
          "en": "And there we have got two important things to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 306.93,
          "en": "The first important thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 306.93,
          "end": 309.17,
          "en": "is that in our project view here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 309.17,
          "end": 311.87,
          "en": "by clicking on this folder and then on this icon here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 313.15,
          "end": 315.23,
          "en": "you expand this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 315.23,
          "end": 317.473,
          "en": "and then go to the info.plist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 318.61,
          "end": 319.73,
          "en": "And now there you'll find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 319.73,
          "end": 322.82,
          "en": "this App Transport Security Settings key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 322.82,
          "end": 325.59,
          "en": "This kind of controls how iOS controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 325.59,
          "end": 328.7,
          "en": "to which web pages or web service your app may talk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 328.7,
          "end": 332.85,
          "en": "and by default, it only allows access to HTTPS servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 332.85,
          "end": 334.633,
          "en": "So SSL secure servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 335.53,
          "end": 336.81,
          "en": "That's a good default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 336.81,
          "end": 338.18,
          "en": "but you might have some exceptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 338.18,
          "end": 340.53,
          "en": "which you can add here and one exception",
          "zh": ""
        },
